{"id":"ac08d903-dbeb-4134-880b-c962e3595a8d","audio_id":"41a47ae1-9364-4f2d-99ce-a42765c57c63","status":"complete","created_at":"2026-11-05T01:21:53Z","answer":"It sounds like a fairly easy-to-repeat toddler hook: the tune is very short and repetitive, and the pulse is light and bouncy. The vocal is bright, high, polished, and feminine-sounding rather than strongly childlike; the backing stays sparse. The key fruit words and “yum” are reported as clear, though the arrangement and delivery feel quite polished, so the hook may come across more produced than spontaneous. There is a brief lead-in before the vocal, and the ending resolves cleanly rather than cutting off. This is a promising audition, not an automatic final approval.

